Below are the most useful columns for this task and the filtering logic they enable.

column name : potential usage / condition
• `reference_name` : keep only chromosome 17 → `reference_name = '17'`  
• `start_position` : coordinate we finally need to report  
• `reference_bases` : keep only reference allele “C” → `reference_bases = 'C'`  
• `alternate_bases.alt` : keep only alternate allele “T” → `ab.alt = 'T'`  
• `alternate_bases.vep.SYMBOL` : find variants that fall in BRCA1 → `v.SYMBOL = 'BRCA1'`  
• `alternate_bases.vep.Consequence` : keep only missense variants  
  (the string may contain several consequences separated by “&”)  
  → `REGEXP_CONTAINS(v.Consequence, r'\bmissense_variant\b')`

